<title>PHILIPPINES: BPI foreign ownership cap raised to 40 pct.</title>
<headline>BPI foreign ownership cap raised to 40 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The government has approved the request of the Bank of the Philippine Islands to increase the limit of foreign ownership in the bank to 40 percent from 30 percent, a statement from the Philippine Stock Exchange said on Monday.</p>
<p>This would allow foreign portfolio investors to buy more BPI shares. BPI had previously disclosed that it had already reached the maximum limit of 30 percent.</p>
<p>-- Manila newsroom 63 2 841-8937 fax 8176267</p>
